                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Quiet (on the page): transparent, 1 px --color-danger-border, label Inter 15/600 --color-danger, height 48 (44 mobile), always ends in “…” because it opens a dialog. Hover adds --color-danger-tint fill. Confirm (inside the dialog only): fill --color-danger, white label Inter 16/600, height 52, hover --color-danger-hover. It names the consequence (“Smazat účet”, not “OK”), sits after “Zrušit”, and never takes the default focus. When typed confirmation is required it stays disabled (track fill + disabled text) until the text matches. Pending: “Mažu…”, busy, disabled. Dialog lists use minus-circle in --color-danger for what is removed and check in --color-action for what stays.",
